# Update the UI

**Verify:** counter increment patches `#counter`; a command returns empty SSE to Datastar and 204 otherwise.

Spell every route as `@method:role(path)`. Role-first forms are **removed**.

## Choose a shape

| Goal | Declaration | Browser result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Read an HTML fragment | `@get:fragment("path")` | Finite `datastar-patch-elements` |
| Replace HTML after a mutation | `@post:fragment("path")` | Finite `datastar-patch-elements` |
| Perform a write, no representation | `@post:command("path")` | Empty SSE to Datastar; 204 otherwise |
| Stream shared HTML | `@get:live("path")` | Long-lived SSE at that path |

There is no default method. Mutation fragments and commands also allow
`@put`, `@patch`, and `@delete`; the other method/role pairs are rejected.

Canonical one-shot: [Counter](/examples/counter/).
Canonical stream: [Live counter](/examples/live-counter/).
Complete matrix: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

## Wire the button

```rocci
<button data-on:click=@post("/actions/inc")>Inc</button>
```

`@post("/path")` is a Rocci action (Roc string, double quotes). A second
argument is a list of Datastar options. Quoted `"@post('…')"` is opaque
Datastar JS, not a Rocci action.

For row-specific URLs, make the attribute a Roc expression. A static quoted
string does not interpolate a `@for` binder.

Do not morph the same `id` from both a finite fragment and a live stream.
Commands return `{}` and carry no success representation.

**Related:** [Datastar as transport](/docs/concepts/datastar-as-transport/),
[One-shot versus live](/docs/concepts/one-shot-versus-live/).
